From babe2a3a1b1b57a71df1c4fb9a35c0b3048a5b63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:59:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] orchestration: remove the Node launcher; workflows run
 through codemod workflow run -w

The Rust CLI now builds and runs TypeScript workflows, so the Node
launcher (bin/codemod-workflow.mjs, register-ts.mjs, host/cli.ts), its
runtime registry, the esbuild/TypeScript build step, the Node bundle
cache and the child-process timings go away, with the standalone
orchestration-quickjs-host binary (the crate stays as the CLI's host
library). Artifact types move to core/artifacts.ts; esbuild and
typescript become dev dependencies.

Specs that covered the removed code are deleted; their rules now live in
crates/cli/tests (typescript_workflow, jssg_parity, typescript_timings)
and crates/orchestration-build/tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
